# A 190 N push on the flange (link 6, 50 mm out along its z) while the
# drives hold the arm (absolute encoders: no phasing). Without friction
# the links are in static balance: every gear torque changes by -J^T f
# (arm.gres = change + J^T f ~ 0; J2 takes ~180 Nm, J3 ~90 Nm). The drives
# hold without a fault; the links deflect by the gear elasticity only.
@program arm/arm_sim
@args arm/arcmate/arcmate.arm
fric 1 0 0 0 0
fric 2 0 0 0 0
fric 3 0 0 0 0
fric 4 0 0 0 0
fric 5 0 0 0 0
fric 6 0 0 0 0
home 0 20 10 30 -60 0
lcnc 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1
run 1.5
mark
force 6 100 -50 -150 0 0 0.05
run 1.0
print gres jtf ferr fault
@expect arm.jtf2 > 150
@expect max|arm.gres1| < 0.5
@expect max|arm.gres2| < 0.5
@expect max|arm.gres3| < 0.5
@expect max|arm.gres4| < 0.2
@expect max|arm.gres5| < 0.2
@expect max|arm.gres6| < 0.2
@expect max|arm.ferr2| < 0.15
@expect max arm.fault2 == 0
@expect max arm.fault3 == 0
@reject ^ERROR
